{"ref":"BDB, כֵּן⁶","hw":"כֵּן⁶","html":"† III. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">כֵּן</span></big>  <strong>n.m. base, pedestal, office (</strong>NH <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּנָּה</span>; Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּנְתָּא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܟܰܢܳܐ</span> <strong>)</strong>—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">כ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 33:23\" href=\"/Isaiah.33.23\">Is 33:23</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:31\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.31\">1 K 7:31</a> (but v. infr.); sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּנּוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:18\" href=\"/Exodus.30.18\">Ex 30:18</a> + 11 times; <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּנֶּ֑ךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 40:13\" href=\"/Genesis.40.13\">Gn 40:13</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּנִּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 41:13\" href=\"/Genesis.41.13\">41:13</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  lit. <em>base, pedestal</em>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:31\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.31\">1 K 7:31</a> (like) the work of <em>a pedestal</em> (Th VB), according to Sta<sup>ZAW iii, 1883, 161, 162</sup> <span dir=\"rtl\">מַעֲשֵׂה־כֵן</span> is in wrong place, being orig. part of a gloss to v <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:35\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.35\">35</a>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">כ׳</span> in v <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.29\">29</a> = <em>thus</em>, or is textual error;—<span dir=\"rtl\">כֵּן־תָּרְנָם</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 33:23\" href=\"/Isaiah.33.23\">Is 33:23</a> <em>the base</em> (<em>support</em> or <em>socket</em>) <em>of their mast</em> (so Thes and most); especially of base of laver of tabernacle <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:18\" href=\"/Exodus.30.18\">Ex 30:18</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:28\" href=\"/Exodus.30.28\">28</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 31:9\" href=\"/Exodus.31.9\">31:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 35:16\" href=\"/Exodus.35.16\">35:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 38:8\" href=\"/Exodus.38.8\">38:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 39:39\" href=\"/Exodus.39.39\">39:39</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 40:11\" href=\"/Exodus.40.11\">40:11</a> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 8:11\" href=\"/Leviticus.8.11\">Lv 8:11</a> (all P).<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>office, place</em> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 40:13\" href=\"/Genesis.40.13\">Gn 40:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 41:13\" href=\"/Genesis.41.13\">41:13</a> (both E); hence (late) <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל־כַּנּוֹ</span> <em>in his place</em> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 11:20\" href=\"/Daniel.11.20\">Dn 11:20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 11:21\" href=\"/Daniel.11.21\">21</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 11:38\" href=\"/Daniel.11.38\">38</a> (i.e. in his stead, as his successor, cf. Germ. <em>an seiner Stelle</em>); <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל</span> om. v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 11:7\" href=\"/Daniel.11.7\">7</a>.","next":"BDB, כְּנַנְיָ֫הוּ","prev":"BDB, כנן"}